    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308">

                <pb facs="0450" n="380" xml:id="pg380"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 205.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-08-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 25, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of August the 6th (No. 179)
                    has been received. No further proceeding will be taken, in the direction
                    heretofore intimated by this government, in regard to New Granada, until the
                    views of the French and British governments shall have been received. It is
                    hoped that they will not long be delayed.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
